The encoder, the annex-b framing and the stdout protocol are the hive's own:
where simfb writes length-prefixed JPEG, simscreen writes the same raw h264
byte stream that `adb exec-out screenrecord --output-format=h264 -` writes, so
the seat pane decodes an iPhone exactly as it decodes an Android emulator.
